"""Tests for the {{ module_title }} module.

Kept as a package so pytest resolves these files under the same package path
the tests import from. Drop this file and the module gets imported twice under
two names.

``InMemory{{ Module }}Repository`` lives here rather than in one of the test
modules because both of them need it and neither should import the other. It
imports the domain and nothing else, which is what lets
``test_{{ module }}_domain.py`` stay free of the framework.

It is also the second adapter for the port, and worth reading as one. If it
ever stops fitting in a screenful, the port has grown wider than the
application layer actually needs.
"""

